iven by ${y}^{′}=(x-a)(x-b).$ Find the value of $a+b.$" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322947 1113 #uuid "69d6e7a9-706b-5fd1-9cdb-c1c105740396" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322947 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/012fe788fa1ac778b361fe62c3f70344546c6c5008fa6dcce536cc721d4ba5e9.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-2$ and $x=1,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nSo, our differential equation must be\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=-2,b=1$ and $a+b=-1.$" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322949 13194139534963 true] [17592186322948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322950 13194139534963 true] [17592186322948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322951 13194139534963 true] [17592186322948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322952 13194139534963 true] [17592186322948 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322953 13194139534963 true] [17592186322948 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534963 true] [17592186322948 1041 "selection" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322948 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322953 13194139534963 true] [17592186322948 1110 #uuid "da6d3baa-2837-5d69-8c1a-a590f7d12d66" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322949 1034 "3" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534963 true] [17592186322949 1111 #uuid "7aa57027-823c-5372-ab48-db66485a5653" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322950 1034 "1" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534963 true] [17592186322950 1111 #uuid "f6e45191-06df-5032-a444-b262dcdde220" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322951 1034 "-3" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322951 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534963 true] [17592186322951 1111 #uuid "c4b4ee96-db63-5058-9321-6f3ea9a1f80a" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322952 1034 "4" 13194139534963 true] [1759218