61782e1fdab4cd182d5ee.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=0$ and $x=3,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-x(x-3)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=9-{x}^{2}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not evaluate to zero at both $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=x(x-2)(x-3)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $x=3,$ but it also evaluates to zero when $x=2,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322963 13194139534963 true] [17592186322962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322964 13194139534963 true] [17592186322962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322965 13194139534963 true] [17592186322962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322966 13194139534963 true] [17592186322962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322967 13194139534963 true] [17592186322962 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534963 true] [17592186322962 1041 "selection" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322962 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322964 13194139534963 true] [17592186322962 1110 #uuid "03e974ba-dc66-5951-b168-9d91c0bd6458" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322963 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322963 1111 #uuid "bf563491-ad5a-5ac9-8788-6b9efece0562" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322964 1034 "I only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322964 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322964 1111 #uuid "dde4f0ad-0037-5b3c-b516-43f3115b2b57" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322965 1034 "III only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322965 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322965 1111 #uuid "53c69429-a62d-5993-8ffa-eb0da87a19bc" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322966 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322966 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322966 1111 #uuid "92c94912-a0b4-54b4-b3a3-47eec8638466" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322967 1034 "II only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322967 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322967 1111 #uuid "4784a473-5aa5-5c3d-b30c-6c731088b658" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322968 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322969 13194139534963 true] [17592186322968 1089 "q-115719" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322968 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534963 true] [17592186322968 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/170ddea2148f369d4feedd14540f234d7946bb6670d1ca6eb4c4ebbbb086a760.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=(x+3)(x+7)$\n- ${y}^{′}=x(x+3)$\n- ${y}^{′}=(x+3)(x+5)$" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322968 1113 #uuid "9e78b269-9005-5d97-be46-7b9aca10039f" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322968 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/cf77e09457cd6b53da801a6eb876a79712935eba623c851a5b6dafa58887a076.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-3$ and $x=-7,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(x+3)(x+7)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-7$ and $x=-3.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=x(x+3)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not evaluate to zero at $x=-7,$ and also evaluates to zero when $x=0,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(x+3)(x+5)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ but it also evaluates to zero when $x=-5,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322970 13194139534963 true] [17592186322969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322971 13194139534963 true] [17592186322969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322972 13194139534963 true] [17592186322969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322973 13194139534963 true] [17592186322969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322974 13194139534963 true] [17592186322969 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534963 true] [17592186322969 1041 "selection" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322969 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322971 13194139534963 true] [17592186322969 1110 #uuid "a0541524-54d2-5ea2-83d0-1a3f50440fae" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322970 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322970 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322970 1111 #uuid "9857310d-32ac-5e22-9c93-b0a51995bdc8" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322971 1034 "I only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322971 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322971 1111 #uuid "528a6458-f976-505a-9266-f4a34e1a8df0" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322972 1034 "III only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322972 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322972 1111 #uuid "52345efd-1752-59f3-95a3-62146364ff65" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322973 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322973 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322973 1111 #uuid "dd1ef709-3fbc-546d-9ce7-8ced2627c198" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322974 1034 "II only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322974 1111 #uuid "6e860563-08e1-59dc-8636-5664bc60dcb1" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322975 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322976 13194139534963 true] [17592186322975 1089 "q-115751" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322975 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534963 true] [17592186322975 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/2552222c6a0be1b1bf1e67a66b4906bb735c2d974d724d3e25e988d15388c696.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{8}{x+1}$\n- ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322975 1113 #uuid "5c45382e-150e-5edb-b139-4af7e110daac" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322975 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/eb1303132a4fe6a26c85b4733a3039a52109b4c49408e1c82038d71885d27f70.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The solution curves have the vertical asymptote $x=-1.$\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side approaches $\\pm \\infty $ as $x\\to -1,$ but it also approaches $\\pm \\infty $ as $x\\to 1,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{8}{x+1}$ gives the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{8}{x+1}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$ does *not* give the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}=-\\frac{x}{(1+\\frac{1}{x})}\\to ∓\\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation do not become horizontal as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322977 13194139534963 true] [17592186322976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322978 13194139534963 true] [17592186322976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322979 13194139534963 true] [17592186322976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322980 13194139534963 true] [17592186322976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322981 13194139534963 true] [17592186322976 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534963 true] [17592186322976 1041 "selection" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322976 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322981 13194139534963 true] [17592186322976 1110 #uuid "c203b590-c954-5726-98e3-886eb268566a" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322977 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322977 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322977 1111 #uuid "0791d30d-e8ac-5c40-9c1e-b6e9b05bd55d" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322978 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322978 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322978 1111 #uuid "68bab059-fafc-54bc-af24-3866220626ee" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322979 1034 "I only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322979 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322979 1111 #uuid "e82d5972-64d3-5a30-b2a7-a205ff620ef2" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322980 1034 "III only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322980 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322980 1111 #uuid "4b661b36-817d-51d6-a9b1-df6e856ecd27" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322981 1034 "II only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322981 1111 #uuid "2783c7c6-b2a3-5273-8e88-2968f3f84258" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322982 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322983 13194139534963 true] [17592186322982 1089 "q-115813" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322982 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534963 true] [17592186322982 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/5a2a2b4b141f4f0c250e4865b174b9eb32b1ed4ab94cc6ebd074131673d5712c.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=-2{x}^{2}-4x-2$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}+2x+1$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}-1$" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322982 1113 #uuid "1cdd2071-3572-5d87-bf79-9e3a992ff987" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322982 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/69465ce0573d7b6deac631663766a5dd1c90afa29eeb0c5286cb5ef1f7ee1153.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope field is zero along the line $x=-1.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on this line.\n\n- Second, the line $x=-1$ divides the plane into $2$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $2$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2{x}^{2}-4x-2=-2(x+1)^{2}\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-1,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+2x+1=(x+1)^{2}\n$$\n\ngives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-1=(x+1)(x-1)\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-1$ and $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322984 13194139534963 true] [17592186322983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322985 13194139534963 true] [17592186322983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322986 13194139534963 true] [17592186322983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322987 13194139534963 true] [17592186322983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322988 13194139534963 true] [17592186322983 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534963 true] [17592186322983 1041 "selection" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322983 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322988 13194139534963 true] [17592186322983 1110 #uuid "d7cef83a-903c-5eeb-a517-b362405e9050" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322984 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322984 1111 #uuid "1b7cedd6-9f5d-5fd0-9ae1-9d68dd04e8a4" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322985 1034 "I only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322985 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322985 1111 #uuid "c55827d4-022b-5bd7-b813-e5419984bc4c" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322986 1034 "III only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322986 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322986 1111 #uuid "ef2f1d42-3783-5fea-80aa-5283f5cdafd0" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322987 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322987 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322987 1111 #uuid "0ac9c0a5-e8af-54ae-a66f-2394f60aebfd" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322988 1034 "II only" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534963 true] [17592186322988 1111 #uuid "38425ced-3908-5671-ab4c-2164d3556e87" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322989 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322990 13194139534963 true] [17592186322989 1089 "q-115846" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322989 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534963 true] [17592186322989 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/b67f4648af37df7332a42a671fd8c3f7b0d7a8f626dc3ed9c4f32c1bb633f258.png)\n\nThe diagram shown above is the slope field for which of the following differential equations?" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322989 1113 #uuid "98ce449b-be7b-52eb-a7f7-5eaea5676c55" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322989 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044310/assets/ef7114aaf0f2cc275b79fe312ac6e99bda2bf07667eaa4ccfaae3920538381b5.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope field is zero along the lines $x=0$ and $x=1.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nOf the given equations, the only two that satisfy this condition are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}=2{x}^{2}(1-x),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x=x(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, the lines $x=0$ and $x=1$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions is easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<0$ | $0<x<1$ | $x>1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↗$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nOf the two remaining options, the only one that gives this behavior is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}.$" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322991 13194139534963 true] [17592186322990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322992 13194139534963 true] [17592186322990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322993 13194139534963 true] [17592186322990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322994 13194139534963 true] [17592186322990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322995 13194139534963 true] [17592186322990 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534963 true] [17592186322990 1041 "selection" 13194139534963 true] [17592186322990 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322994 13194139534963 true] [17592186322990 1110 #uuid "2718120b-4462-54ac-bc13-1da56dd43a88" 13194139534